-- title:
--   One smooth compact approximation sequence for countably many window norms
-- statement:
--   Let $(\mu_n)_{n\ge0}$ be an increasing sequence of Borel measures on $\mathbf R$, each finite on compact sets. Suppose a complex-valued function $f$ belongs to $L^2(\mu_n)$ for every $n$.
--
--   There is a single sequence $g_k\in C_c^\infty(\mathbf R;\mathbf C)$, each belonging to every $L^2(\mu_n)$, such that
--   $$\lim_{k\to\infty}\|f-g_k\|_{L^2(\mu_n)}=0
--   \qquad\text{for every fixed }n.$$
--
--   This is simultaneous approximation in the topology generated by all the individual window norms. It does not assert convergence of a uniform supremum over $n$. The theorem supplies the diagonal approximation step needed to identify a complete weighted intersection with the completion of its smooth test functions.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Norm convergence is expressed using the extended-valued $L^2$ seminorm; the stated membership hypotheses and conclusions ensure the errors have finite seminorms.
-- source:
--   Auxiliary theorem for the compact-window repair of A. M. Masullo, The Music of the Primes, Definition 9.2.2.1 and Lemma 9.2.2.2(3), printed pp. 412-413, and Proposition 9.2.2.4, p. 414. Frozen source: https://math216.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/the-music-of-the-primes.pdf . This develops Yi's proposed compact-window replacement (mission comment a96ab6a0-9f70-4b3f-ab3e-8c7e38a823f2), after the accepted completeness theorem fea3483f-d6b8-43ba-95b4-3acb3895e88f. It is an explicitly stated repair, not a claim that the original uniform supremum is finite. Smooth approximation input: Mathlib, Analysis/Normed/Lp/SmoothApprox.lean, MeasureTheory.MemLp.exist_eLpNorm_sub_le, at pinned revision 0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474. The countable diagonal argument is supplied here.

import Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Lp.SmoothApprox
import Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Basic
import Mathlib.Topology.Instances.ENNReal.Lemmas

set_option autoImplicit false
open MeasureTheory Set Filter Topology
open scoped ENNReal ContDiff

theorem MasulloRepair.simultaneous_smooth_L2_approximation (μ : ℕ → Measure ℝ)
    [∀ n, IsFiniteMeasureOnCompacts (μ n)] (hμ : Monotone μ)
    (f : ℝ → ℂ) (hf : ∀ n, MemLp f 2 (μ n)) :
    ∃ g : ℕ → ℝ → ℂ,
      (∀ k, HasCompactSupport (g k) ∧ ContDiff ℝ ∞ (g k)) ∧
      (∀ n k, MemLp (g k) 2 (μ n)) ∧
      ∀ n, Tendsto (fun k => eLpNorm (f - g k) 2 (μ n)) atTop (𝓝 0) := by sorry
